---
import ContentShell from '../layouts/ContentShell.astro'
import { url } from '../data/slugs'

const UPDATED = '19 August 2026'
const CONTACT = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL ?? 'hello@punehire.com'

const mail = (subject: string) => `mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}`

const description =
  'How to reach the person who maintains Punehire: corrections, a missing company, ' +
  'a listing that should come down, and how long a reply actually takes.'
---

<ContentShell
  title="Contact and corrections | Punehire"
  description={description}
  path="/contact/"
  h1="Contact and corrections"
  lede="One email address, read by the person who maintains this site. There is no form here, because there is no server behind this site to receive one."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Contact', href: '/contact/' }]}
  narrow
>
  <p>
    <a class="apply" href={mail('Punehire')}>{CONTACT}</a>
  </p>
  <p class="small muted">
    That link opens your own mail client. Nothing is submitted through this page, and no
    contact details are stored anywhere on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>What to write about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A company in the wrong area.</strong> Areas are assigned by hand from a curated
      list, so this is exactly the kind of error worth reporting. Send the company and the
      correct area, and a link if you have one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A missing startup.</strong> If a Pune startup should be tracked here, send its
      name and careers page URL. Companies with a public feed from Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby,
      Workday, SmartRecruiters or Recruitee can be added with live roles; the rest can be
      listed with a careers link only.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A role that should not be here.</strong> Filled, withdrawn, never in Pune,
      posted by mistake. Send the page URL.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A removal or takedown request.</strong> See below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A listing that looks like a scam.</strong> Anything asking a candidate for money
      to apply. Send the URL and it comes down while it is checked, not after.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anything factually wrong on any page.</strong> Including this one.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Removals and takedowns</h2>
  <p>
    If you are the employer, or you act for them, and you want a job listing or an entire
    company page removed from this site, that request is honoured. No argument, no form, no
    justification needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="apply" href={mail('Removal request')}>Send a removal request</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    Include the page URL or the company name, and say whether you want a single role removed
    or the company excluded from the index entirely. An exclusion is permanent: the company is
    added to a do-not-crawl list, so it does not reappear the next time its feed is read.
  </p>
  <p>
    Removal requests are dealt with before anything else in the inbox. The listing is taken
    out at the next build, which runs every six hours. If a request is urgent, say so in the
    subject line and the build can be triggered immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>How long a reply takes</h2>
  <p>
    This site is maintained by one person alongside other work. Removal and scam reports are
    handled within a day or two. Corrections and additions are usually read within a few days
    and applied in a batch, because most of them mean editing the curated company list rather
    than replying to an email. Every message is read; not every message gets a reply.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once a fix lands in the data, the site picks it up at the next scheduled build, within six
    hours.
  </p>

  <h2>What this address is not for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Applications.</strong> We do not accept CVs, and one sent here will not reach any
      employer. Apply on the company's own site, through the apply button on the role's page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Job-hunt help.</strong> No referrals, no introductions, no interview coaching.
      This is an index, not a placement service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Paid placement.</strong> Listings cannot be bought, promoted or ranked higher.
      There is no price, so please do not ask for one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Guest posts, link exchanges and SEO offers.</strong> These are deleted unread.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={url.about()}>How this works</a> covers where the listings come from, why some
    companies show a careers link and no roles, and the known limits of the area, experience
    and remote fields. Several common corrections are already answered there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Also: <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>,
    <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>,
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="small muted">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
</ContentShell>

<style>
  h2 { margin-top: 1.9em; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.15em; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  li { margin-bottom: .55em; }
</style>
